 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.0
+
+- Added (rightkit#634, additive, feature `tokio`, off by default): `async_io` with `read_json_line_async`, `read_json_line_opts_async`, `read_json_line_or_oversized_opts_async`, `read_json_line_or_oversized_observed_async`, `read_line_bytes_async`, `write_json_line_async` and `write_json_line_flush_async`, over `AsyncBufRead + Unpin` and `AsyncWrite + Unpin`. Same limit, bounded-resync, blank-line, oversized-value, observer and error behaviour as the blocking functions (the line loop is a port of `next_line`); the futures are `Send`. Depends only on tokio `io-util`: no runtime, task or timer. Tests are in `src/async_io.rs`. Not compiled when written.
+- BREAKING (rightkit#734 part b, minor bump for 0.x): `wire::WireError` has a new public field `details: Option<serde_json::Value>`, so code that builds `WireError { .. }` as a struct literal must add `details: None` or use `WireError::new` / `WireError::retryable`. On the wire it is written only when present and read tolerantly: a frame without it, or with `null`, parses with `None`, and a 0.2 peer ignores it. New: `WireError::with_details`, `WireError::details`, `WireError::detail(key)`. Tests are in `src/wire.rs`. Not compiled when written.
+
 ## 0.2.1
 
 - Added (rightkit#190, additive): `length_prefixed::read_frame_bytes_deadline` and `write_frame_bytes_deadline` move one length-prefixed frame over any `Read` or `Write` before an absolute `Instant`, waiting through a readiness callback (`Ready`: given the time left, returns whether the stream is ready). For transports that are not a plain descriptor or overlapped handle (the descriptor-based `read_frame_deadline` and `write_frame_deadline` from 0.2.0 are unchanged). Same wire format and error mapping as `deadline`: a deadline is `FrameError::TimedOut { partial_bytes }` (0 means still on a frame boundary), a zero length or empty body is `Io(InvalidData)`, a length above the limit is `TooLarge` (a write sends nothing; a read leaves the body unread, close the stream), and an end of stream, including a clean one between frames, is `Io(UnexpectedEof)` (message `peer closed before a frame header` for the clean case), never `Ok(None)`. `Interrupted` and `WouldBlock` retry until the deadline. Tests: `tests/deadline_generic.rs`. Not compiled when written.
